# The client certificate and key must never reach an image layer. Deleting them in a later RUN is
# not enough: the earlier COPY layer still carries the file, and a later layer only adds a whiteout
# marker, so 'docker save' recovers the key from any published image. Keeping them out of the build
# context is what actually prevents that. They are mounted from a Kubernetes secret at runtime.
#
# To bake the certificates into an image on purpose, remove these two lines and add a COPY of them
# as etc/breeze.crt and etc/breeze.key, see the alternative in README.md.
breeze/runtime/etc/*.crt
breeze/runtime/etc/*.key

# the installer archive itself, unpacked next to it
*.tgz

.DS_Store
